## ACTIVE TASK

### D1 — Account Seller Overview — VERIFY & SHIP

- Branch `d1-account-seller-overview`, cut from `origin/main` at
  `662c33d158901309bf32eb87438a4015d39bcac9`. No migration, schema, RLS,
  production write, payment, payout or provider change.
- The audit confirmed the five premises before any edit: `/vendite` already had
  a real Seller Dashboard; it already used exactly one order read and one
  listing read; `riepilogoVenditore()` already derived active listings, orders
  awaiting the seller, completed sales and their value; that value is not a
  balance, an incasso or a payout; `/account` still rendered `Certificazioni`.
  The foundation was reused, not rebuilt.
- New file `frontend-next/src/app/account/attivita-vendita.tsx`, an
  Account-specific client component, colocated the way `app/vendi/
  bottle-selector.tsx` already is. It performs the same two reads as `/vendite`
  — `createOrderService(client).vendite()` and
  `createListingService(client).mieiAnnunci()` — in one `Promise.all`, and
  passes both to `riepilogoVenditore()`. There is no per-KPI query, no `.from()`
  or `.rpc()` of its own, no `profiles` read and no duplicated KPI rule.
- The four KPIs reuse the existing `Kpi` component and the dashboard's own
  labels and hints, including `Prezzo venditore, non un incassato` for the
  monetary one. No `Saldo`, `Disponibile`, `Incassato`, `Guadagno`, `Payout`,
  `Balance`, `Credito` or `Prelievo` semantic was introduced.
- Loading, zero and error are three distinct states. While the reads are in
  flight nothing numeric is rendered, so no false zero is shown as if it were
  data. Zero activity renders four real zeros and is a valid state. A failed
  order read renders a compact generic sentence inside that section only and
  does not expose the service message.
- The section exists for any authenticated account. No role, no
  `seller_verificato`, no certification and no listing count decides whether it
  is shown.
- The profile-editing module is untouched and cannot be broken by the section:
  `page-client.tsx` imports neither service nor the dashboard module, holds no
  state for those reads, and renders `<AttivitaVendita />` as a sibling card
  after the form.
- The old `Certificazioni` card, its `RigaCertificazione` row component and the
  now-unused `vociCertificazione`, `VoceCertificazione`, `ShieldCheck` and
  `Clock` imports were removed from the Account UI only. `certificazioni.ts`,
  its tests, `my_certifications`, `profile_certifications` and the profile
  service are unchanged. No professional badge or qualification surface was
  created; Professional Qualifications remains a separate, out-of-scope work
  package.
- VERIFY found one real defect in the BUILD and corrected it.
  `ListingService.mieiAnnunci()` deliberately collapses a failed read and a
  genuinely empty list onto the same `[]`. That contract is right for the
  listing-management surfaces, which show that emptiness; it is wrong as the
  source of a *number*. The Account section consumed it directly, so a failed
  listings read would have rendered `Annunci attivi 0 su 0` as a fact.
- The correction reuses the pattern this same file already established for
  `elenco()` / `elencoConEsito()`: one closure, `leggiMieiAnnunci`, holds the
  single `from("listings")` query with its explicit `.eq("seller_id", user.id)`
  filter; `mieiAnnunci()` keeps its historical collapse for existing consumers
  and `mieiAnnunciConEsito()` returns the undecayed `Result`. No new query, no
  direct query from the Account, no migration, no RLS change. `/vendite` still
  calls `mieiAnnunci()` and its behaviour is unchanged.
- The Account section now writes its KPI state only when *both* reads
  succeeded, and shows its generic in-section message when either fails. No
  PostgreSQL or PostgREST message reaches the page: a listings failure is
  mediated as `Annunci non disponibili.` and the raw error stays in the logs.
- The two `dashboard.test.ts` source assertions on `mieiAnnunci` were re-anchored
  to `leggiMieiAnnunci`, preserving their intent — explicit `seller_id` filter,
  session guard before the table query — and a third pins that both signatures
  descend from that one read.
- VERIFY measured **75 pass / 0 fail / 256 assertions** across
  `app/account/attivita-vendita`, `lib/vendite/dashboard` and
  `services/listing-avatar`; a clean `tsc --noEmit`; full `frontend-next` ESLint
  at **0 errors / 13 warnings**, all pre-existing; and a clean
  `git diff --check`. The full `frontend-next` build succeeded.
- The complete suite measured **893 pass / 0 fail / 17912 assertions across 55
  files** with Bun 1.3.14, identical on two consecutive runs. The CI
  `MIN_TESTS` floor and the `prelaunch-contract` regression assertion were
  raised together from **863** to **893**, and the suite was re-run green
  against the raised floor.
- Browser smoke, Supabase grids, backend and payout runs were deliberately not
  executed: this work package changes no schema, no policy and no production
  state.
- The pre-existing untracked `.wslconfig`, the pre-existing stash and the other
  worktrees remain excluded and untouched.

